= Solution
{parent=5}

Multiply numerator and denominator by the <complex conjugate> $5+4i$:
$$
\frac{3+5i}{5-4i}=\frac{(3+5i)(5+4i)}{25+16}
=\frac{-5+37i}{41}.
$$
The <real part> and <imaginary part> are therefore
$$
\boxed{\operatorname{Re}=-\frac5{41},\qquad\operatorname{Im}=\frac{37}{41}}.
$$

