= Solution
{parent=7}

For this <separable differential equation>, away from $x=1$, separation gives $\ln|y+1|=\ln|x-1|+C$, or $y+1=K(x-1)$ on a connected interval. The <initial condition> gives $2=-K$, hence
$$
\boxed{y=1-2x}.
$$
The maximal interval containing $x=0$ on which this solves the printed <differential equation> is $\boxed{-\infty<x<1}$. Although the linear formula extends through one, the right-hand side there is $0/0$ and the original equation is undefined. The <equilibrium> solution $y=-1$, lost if one divides by $y+1$, does not satisfy the <initial condition>.

= 8
{parent=Paper 2}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=8}

For independent fair dice, the <probability> of avoiding one on each die is $5/6$. Therefore
$$
\boxed{P(\text{neither is one})=\left(\frac56\right)^2=\frac{25}{36}}.
$$
The <complement of an event> gives
$$
\boxed{P(\text{at least one is one})=1-\frac{25}{36}=\frac{11}{36}}.
$$

